      "id": "claim_91a3156aafb84da997c75663c9c5636a",
      "statement": "Each shipped format blueprint is two files with the same stem — the .gadget archive holding code and bindings, and a .json sidecar holding the curated blueprintId, title, description, output, author, and revision — and the installer writes sidecar values over whatever the archive carries.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/format-blueprints/README.md#L16-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0a1dd6897f6708fd0c0921d3d2a0d87f80dc238b25f9074112c01f5fa82cd586:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_de6d0e70f4164557a53f819e7cb2ff12",
      "statement": "Updating a format's code goes through pnpm import:format-blueprint, which rewrites the archive and bumps the sidecar revision — revision is the reinstall trigger for the one input (archive bytes) the install fingerprint cannot see, and the script's bindings line flags when instantiating users will be asked for new connections.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/format-blueprints/README.md#L36-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5210a1695d85b36bb81584dc4db814739ab23d829cca19c6e35146ed1392c503:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_79f532e12aa34af8894f782a297a48ae",
      "statement": "Title, description, and author edits require no revision bump because the installed-version fingerprint is blueprintId@revision plus a fingerprint of the presentation fields, so any change there triggers reinstallation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/format-blueprints/README.md#L26-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:50d4b84c47657f6f867d6c6bfc0d0736a41dcdf0c8472a02d3ac929c6ee274a5:"
