    {
      "id": "claim_cf7721bc8950463d935d281a9b9f1953",
      "statement": "Installing a bundled blueprint parses it through the ordinary archive reader (a corrupt bundled file fails like a bad upload), writes R2 content before KV metadata (an orphan object is harmless, metadata-without-content is broken), and skips-and-logs individual failures so one bad archive cannot deny the deployment the other formats.",
